next=(all 20 phases done; open work is listed below)

notes:
- transport = TCP + u32 BE length prefix; TLS via the `tls` feature
  (tokio-rustls/ring, self-signed generation with `generate-cert`)
  QUIC would be a transport swap; the framing layer is independent
- serve(listener, state, security) / serve_tls(..., acceptor)
  handle_connection is generic over AsyncRead+AsyncWrite
- auth = shared bearer token in RegisterNode, constant-time compare,
  RegisterRejected on failure
- agent identity persists in <data dir>/aethermesh/node-id
- config: TOML (ControllerConfig / AgentConfig), CLI flags override,
  deny_unknown_fields; examples in examples/*.toml
- observability: MeshMetrics counters in MeshState + Prometheus text form,
  periodic metrics log line in the controller binary
- Controller::new(scheduler, transport, catalog)
    .with_chunk_size(n).with_compression(p).with_data_reuse(b).with_retry(r)
  retry: unreachable/timeout only; a task that ran and failed is not retried
- benchmark: `run --mode baseline|aethermesh` and `compare`
  in-process measurement (real codec + real executor, no sockets)

open work (not started):
- no task submission CLI (library API only)
- parallel chunk transfer (design supports it; transports send sequentially)
- bandwidth/latency are caller-supplied; nothing measures them yet
- cloud SDK adapters (AWS/GCP/Azure/K8s) behind CloudProvider
- client certificates / per-node credentials (single shared token today)
